  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"FDX1 DMS - Tsvekov lab,\" made available on Figshare, has garnered minimal initial engagement, with only three views and no downloads or citations documented as of now. However, it has been re-used in at least one biomedical article, indicating some academic interest.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2025, the dataset from the Tsvekov lab is categorized as 'open access' and features concepts integral to various fields, including environmental science, computer science, and engineering. While no author details are publicly available beside Jason Kwon, who serves as the corresponding author, the dataset may support a wide range of research applications due to its interdisciplinary nature.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite being newly released, the dataset has not achieved widespread visibility or engagement, as evidenced by its current lack of citations or mentions in popular academic databases such as OpenAlex and Europe PMC, apart from a single reuse documented in a biomedical article. This limited reach might reflect the challenges that newer datasets often face in gaining traction within the scholarly community.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The absence of direct social online mentions, such as on platforms like Reddit or Twitter, further signals a need for increased promotional efforts to boost awareness and utilization of the dataset among researchers. Nonetheless, the dataset remains accessible through its registration on prominent data repositories, ensuring that it can be readily integrated into future research endeavors.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Looking ahead, the potential for future citations and engagements may improve as the field continues to evolve and as researchers become more aware of the resources available in the Tsvekov lab dataset. Enhancements in outreach and visibility strategies could foster a vibrant discourse surrounding its applications in relevant scientific domains.</p>",
